1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:04,867
The same tree: blossoms in spring,

2
00:00:04,917 --> 00:00:06,622
leaves in summer, snow in winter.

3
00:00:06,672 --> 00:00:08,431
Every year, the seasons come back.

4
00:00:08,481 --> 00:00:09,704
But why do they change?

5
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:12,152
Noah thinks Earth gets closer

6
00:00:12,202 --> 00:00:13,379
to the Sun in summer.

7
00:00:13,429 --> 00:00:15,833
Mila takes out a globe: look, it's tilted!

8
00:00:15,883 --> 00:00:16,759
That's the key.

9
00:00:17,552 --> 00:00:19,066
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:21,582 --> 00:00:22,039
Mini mode!

11
00:00:22,089 --> 00:00:23,968
Earth goes around the Sun in one year,

12
00:00:24,018 --> 00:00:26,810
and its axis stays tilted, always in the same direction.

13
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,043
So sometimes the North leans toward the Sun,

14
00:00:29,093 --> 00:00:30,717
sometimes it leans away from it.

15
00:00:31,514 --> 00:00:34,977
Leaning toward the Sun, the North gets the rays head-on:

16
00:00:35,027 --> 00:00:37,360
they heat strongly, and days are long.

17
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:38,113
It's summer!

18
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:41,939
Leaning away, the rays come in at a slant and days are short:

19
00:00:41,989 --> 00:00:42,428
winter.

20
00:00:43,238 --> 00:00:45,057
And during the North's summer,

21
00:00:45,107 --> 00:00:48,483
the South leans the other way: down there, it's winter!

22
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:50,277
Six months later, they swap.

23
00:00:51,265 --> 00:00:52,353
What about distance?

24
00:00:52,403 --> 00:00:55,880
Surprise: Earth is even a little closer to the Sun in January,

25
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,473
in the middle of our winter.

26
00:00:57,523 --> 00:00:58,888
Distance hardly matters.

27
00:00:59,671 --> 00:01:01,592
That's why the seasons change.

28
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:06,295
Earth is tilted: the half tilted toward the Sun has summer,

29
00:01:06,345 --> 00:01:07,718
the other half has winter.

30
00:01:08,702 --> 00:01:11,884
With an adult: shine a flashlight on a sheet of paper,

31
00:01:11,934 --> 00:01:13,680
straight on, then at an angle.

32
00:01:13,730 --> 00:01:14,398
At an angle,

33
00:01:14,448 --> 00:01:17,022
the spot is bigger and weaker: like winter!

34
00:01:17,811 --> 00:01:19,561
And why is the sea salty?

35
00:01:19,611 --> 00:01:21,051
The answer tomorrow.
